    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8b814727",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The meme is designed for an audience that may be unfamiliar with the socio-political context of the Amsterdam red light district and is likely to be exposed to misleading or stereotypical portrayals of women in South Asia. The target audience may include individuals who are susceptible to false equivalences, racialized stereotypes, and misogynistic tropes, particularly those who hold or are influenced by anti-Black and Islamophobic views. The meme exploits visual and textual cues to reinforce harmful narratives about women of African descent and South Asian women, suggesting that their appearance or attire is inherently linked to prostitution or moral degradation. The intended audience may also include those who are unaware of the legal and cultural distinctions between Amsterdam’s regulated sex industry and the non-existent 'red light district' in Islamabad, thereby perpetuating misinformation and reinforcing systemic biases.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_76a1979d"
